      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "32a78636ecd441a39f8c8c0a03bdd1f2_28",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "Therefore, the Senior Citizen is willing to reside there after the death of his wife."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "b51450392c2d4fb88ed1500977d6dfc8_29",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "Therefore, the right to residence is to be protected by the competent Authority under the Senior Citizen Act."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "662505e4cacd456d8db2a0bc50fc1feb_30",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "\n6. Close reading of the principles laid down by the Hon'ble Apex Court and the High Courts, there is no ambiguity with reference to the purpose and object sought to be achieved under the provisions of the Senior Citizen Act."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "7c5fdd6cceb3464eb201e1ecc9c876c8_31",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "STA"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "\n7. Section 4 (2) of the Act, enumerates that the obligation of the https://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis children or the relative, as the case may be, to maintain a Senior Citizen extends to the needs of such Citizen, so that Senior Citizen may "
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "60175e9d548f4504b0c53da0476fef68_32",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "Normal Life must be interpreted constructively in the context of the definition for maintenance as stipulated under Section 2 (b) of the Act."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "a96581da9e564b75a2dc704a6136df75_33",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "STA"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "8. The adoption of the phrase normal life Rule 20 (2) (i) of the Maintenance of Senior Citizen Rules, enumerates that it shall be the duty of the District Collector to ensure that life and property of senior citizens of the District are pro"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "ba98b82f5cf344b9866f0e2823b25423_34",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "\nTherefore, 'normal life' includes security and dignity."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "6bcb7d37d1af4b0aaf8b993ca3b294eb_35",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "Thus the 'normal life' as indicated under Section 4(2) of the Act, is not mere life, but a life with security and dignity."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "1a3bdb11faeb42acbbb35a6d35071314_36",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "In the context of Article 21 of the Constitution of India, life includes decent medical facility, residence, food, shelter with dignity and security."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "4398d8fed6f74c7fb0b717df24adce83_37",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "All such combined necessities of human life is falling under the term Normal Life emboldened under Section 4(2) of the Senior Citizen Act."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "fbee7ab5d6044d3ab83a032a2bdc8edc_38",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "Therefore, simply providing food and shelter would be insufficient."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "80fdffc0a0044f38aaa7947276b16c80_39",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "But life includes providing decent medical facilities, food & residence,\nshelter and other requirement with dignity in commensuration with the status of the family and taking into consideration of the living style of the https://www.mhc.tn."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "23aa689a627741978f9e346727cfd4e1_40",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "9. In the present case, the 3rd respondent was holding the post of Chief Engineer (Group-I) post in Tamil Nadu Electricity Board."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "9975e674f70048d392c39eac747a29ea_41",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "Therefore, the lifestyle, he maintained previously is to be protected by the competent Authority under the Senior Citizen Act.\n10."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "6487e409733442069c79e99971007f23_42",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "Therefore, the children defending their case merely on the ground that they are willing to provide food and shelter, cannot be taken as a ground for the purpose of sustaining their claim to retain the property."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "35dd9b4820be45d2b12f2b15c7f2df5d_43",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "In the present case, the property belongs to the 3rd respondent and his deceased wife."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "8d21ce0307764708b7ddf9bda19456d7_44",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "The requirements of the provision complied in its real spirit and the Competent Authorities are bound to protect the interest and the life of the Senior Citizen.\n11. Section 4(3) denotes, the obligation of the children to maintain his or he"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "ffbe919428904d82af3e8c1c9928d0d0_45",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "Therefore, it is an obligation on the part of the children to maintain his or her parents and ensure the parents to lead a normal life."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "d016cf04ab1b4731a79100ec2e0bc872_46",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "In the event of complaint, the Authorities Competent are expected to ensure that the senior citizen and their life and dignity are protected."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "0e575ff192aa4a54bb50a1d4378871fb_47",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "The above provision is to be read in conjunction with the Rules framed under the Act."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "dbe64232a3eb4d4f8aa07a844581faca_48",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "\nS.Kalaiarasan vs The District Collector on 15 April, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/114244593/\n3 12."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "e1d5614cc0864019bb951c78fa43e3fc_49",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "Rule 20 of the Maintenance of Senior Citizen Rules, provide duties and powers of the District Collector."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "b606020108364c77b77b26686b05ec57_50",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "The District Collector is casted upon the duty to ensure that the life and property of citizens of the District are protected and other people to live with security and dignity."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "46a691d34de04dfca203675f016337b0_51",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "Therefore, it is the statutory duty on the part of the District Collector to protect the safety and security of senior citizens in his District."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "54e21dea2e68444e8c4d91d85df31416_52",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "Thus the complaint filed by the senior citizen, cannot be treated lightly."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "a4128a45497c4d328cf12c3ab31dbc9f_53",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "Such complaints are to be enquired into in a pragmatic manner, so as to understand the real grievances of the senior citizen and accordingly, all appropriate actions are to be initiated to provide safety,\nsecurity and to protect the dignity"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "bb6bd12d9a52426096e8d0a067aaf76c_54",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "RATIO"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "13. The 3rd respondent in the present case has no intention to deprive their children to possess the property belongs to him."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "839e52caad544929849c82ba6794d897_55",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "RATIO"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "However, he wants to retain the subject house for his residence, wherein his deceased wife lived."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "5bfe30994ac14ef79fce837fd0a7146f_56",
        "summary_section": "decision",
        "labels": [
          "RPC"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:decision",
          "forbidden_labels:RPC",
          "suspicious_label:rpc"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "https://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "c2ca73fd2f34471e8100c0640826ed9c_57",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "RATIO"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "That being the sentiment, the District Collector has rightly appreciated the claim of the 3rd respondent and allowed the claim by issuing a direction to possess the subject property and further directed the Police Authorities to protect the"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "7406b73c69fb46c581276a062d33a0ec_58",
        "summary_section": "decision",
        "labels": [
          "RPC"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:decision",
          "forbidden_labels:RPC",
          "suspicious_label:rpc"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "14. This Court do not find any infirmity in respect of the order passed by the District Collector."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "a66dfc9584c241b4bc820c9b69c5582d_59",
        "summary_section": "decision",
        "labels": [
          "RPC"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:decision",
          "forbidden_labels:RPC",
          "suspicious_label:rpc"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "The Authorities are directed to protect the life and property of the 3rd respondent as directed by the District Collector."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "32318156249b49d08383bfd18618d585_60",
        "summary_section": "decision",
        "labels": [
          "RPC"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:decision",
          "forbidden_labels:RPC",
          "suspicious_label:rpc"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "15. With the above observations, this Writ Petition stands dismissed."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "a191646688bb42e99b20d3b75ef25d6f_61",
        "summary_section": "decision",
        "labels": [
          "RPC"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:decision",
          "forbidden_labels:RPC",
          "suspicious_label:rpc"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "No costs."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "c279da40717140d1b95c8ba628845b7d_62",
        "summary_section": "decision",
        "labels": [
          "RPC"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:decision",
          "forbidden_labels:RPC",
          "suspicious_label:rpc"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "Consequently,\nconnected miscellaneous petitions are closed."
      }
    ],
